WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:09.690
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:19.810
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.540
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:07.010
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:14.250
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:20.990
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:28.080
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.490
I am Anubituf,
the captain of the Arcus Prima…

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:39.780
…one of the largest airships
in Simulacrum Kyuukoku’s fleet.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.580
Three air squadrons, Simoun chors,
are stationed on the Arcus Prima.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.210
Chor Tempest,
Chor Caput, and Chor Rubor.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:56.340
But Chor Tempest, once prided for
defense and flawless Ri Majons…

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.430
…has lost its high standing and is now
being relegated to reserve status.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.430
And now, as we escort
the Plumbum highland delegation…

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.440
…to international waters, where
a peace conference is scheduled…

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:16.610
…tensions in Chor Tempest over its
new members have sparked a brawl.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:24.120
Chor Tempest has been ordered to
disband as soon as we return to port.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.190
For those with reasons for wanting
to continue flying the Simouns…

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.090
…it is a bitter sentence.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.500
Either way, when it’s time
to journey to the Spring…

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.130
…one can no longer fly a Simoun.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.990
And now the peace
conference is about to begin.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:49.640
<b>Prayer</b>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.650
We understand that your priestesses
are all fluent in Kyuukoku’s language.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.150
But for translating purposes,
wouldn’t just one suffice?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.320
We are not mere interpreters.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.490
We also watch over
this important conference.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.870
And several are needed
for certain ceremonies.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.500
That’s fine.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.090
We should have some of Tempus
Spatium’s priestesses attend as well.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.130
I think that’s a good idea.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.640
They are not merely priestesses…

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.970
…but soldiers too, no?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.560
How long will you snivel?

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.400
Thanks to you, we’ve been disbanded.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.410
We should be crying.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:49.360
But at least now we can
finally stop flying Simouns.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.640
Mamina, what have
you been doing since then?

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.120
You lived with your mother after
your father passed away, correct?

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.010
Tell me about it.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:09.210
I’ve got to keep flying Simouns.
I have to remain a sibylla…

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.520
That’s just like Aer.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.530
You want to go on
being a sibylla too, right?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.030
No way.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.860
Why? As long as you’re a sibylla,
you don’t have to go to the Spring.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.080
That’s the problem.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.710
We all want to go to the Spring,
but since becoming sibyllae…

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:35.370
…we have to take part in this war now
and are unable to go to the Spring.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.750
It’s not like it’s forbidden.
Just quit being a sibylla, right?

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.590
After being finally
chosen after such toil?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:47.660
I do have my pride as a priestess.
Avoiding the front line isn’t an option.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.600
We all have our reasons…

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.390
…but I’ve never seen anyone who
wanted to avoid going to the Spring.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.340
Oh? If you want to see, be my guest.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.400
Here.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.230
What are you doing?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.240
It’s obvious.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.950
This ballroom is where Chor Tempest
socializes. It’s always been that way.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.450
People like the captain
never decided that.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:15.760
But it’s always been
that way, remember?

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.410
You guys never used to come here.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.500
You’re on standby and might
scramble at any time, right?

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.960
Take it easy.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.520
Oh, jeez, I can’t stand this.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.140
Big Sister, why don’t
you come to my room?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.530
Hey, everybody! Big news!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.030
Big news! Big news!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.540
She always seems to be having fun.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.730
It’s been decided that just two
of the highland priestesses…

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:02.110
…will be allowed
to attend the peace conference.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:07.300
Meaning that this priestess here,
Anglas, will not be allowed to attend.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.800
She’ll stay with Chor Tempest
until the conference is over.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.310
Because we’re fellow priestesses?

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.380
We can leave it at that.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:22.480
I’ll be patrolling the conference site.
I hope everything’s clear.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.820
Make sure you don’t offend our guest.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:32.320
The only thing is we don’t
speak the same language…

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.830
I am not fluent, but I can speak a little.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.440
I’ve heard many highland priestesses
are from the border near Kyuukoku.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:51.620
Right, speaking of which, that area’s
tribes travel between the countries.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:57.350
They say our god was once
the same deity that you worship here.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.850
That’s why, um…

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.690
You feel an affinity with us.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.200
The little one is Rimone.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.650
The two on the right are Alty and Kaim.
They’re sisters, you know.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:15.700
That’s Morinas.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:20.030
Rimone, Alty, Kaim, Morinas.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.210
And there…

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.210
Starting from the right, Paraietta,
Dominüra, and Roatreamon.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.720
Paraietta, Dominüra, Roatreamon.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.720
What a lovely name.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.720
It’s a very noble name.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.230
From a venerable family that’s borne
generations of Simoun sibyllae.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.540
And the girl who just spoke up
is Mamina. Next to her is…

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.760
I’m Yun.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.610
And I wish for
a speedy end to the war.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.710
I’m glad to know there will soon
be peace between our countries.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.710
Mamina and Yun.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.120
That’s what I wish for too.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.920
My name’s Floe.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:03.960
Floe.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.460
Let’s see… Who else?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.960
The girl in the very back is Aer.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.550
The only one missing is Neviril.
And that’s everyone.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.470
Pleased to meet you.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.650
Now that introductions are done…

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:23.730
Hey, hold on!

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.560
You’re the only one
she didn’t call by name.

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:35.320
Yeah, she said
everyone’s name but mine.

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.690
Does she have
to say every single name?

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.130
How tedious.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.170
I know it is, but…

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.160
Say, what do you think about this?

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.700
We’re priestesses.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.380
But we turned the Simouns
into weapons of war.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.420
To do that…

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:56.930
In the eyes of normal priestesses
like you, it’s peculiar, isn’t it?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.880
It is very cold in the highlands.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:08.190
We’re blessed by
a compassionate god, but even so…

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.900
Every year, there is a cold snap,
resulting in many deaths.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.900
I am a priestess…

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:20.950
…so I pray that those who have
perished may find bliss in God’s arms.

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:23.810
I know what you mean.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.540
When we first started as sibyllae…

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.460
…I thought we would fly Simouns
in divine ceremonies like that.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.220
You’re right. We should be flying
the Simouns in order to pray…

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.180
What a carefree attitude.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:44.430
You take becoming a sibylla
for granted, so you can say that.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.940
What do you mean by that, Mamina?

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:54.320
If it hadn’t been for this war,
I never could have become a sibylla.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.530
There were only a handful
of young girls in my village.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:08.040
So it wasn’t hard to serve the great
temple as a priestess in training.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.470
But…

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:16.550
U-Um…

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:21.260
When I become a sibylla,
will you fly with me as my pair?

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.230
You? A sibylla?

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:29.270
Sibyllae are selected by Tempus
Spatium. People of humble birth…

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.130
And then that day came.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.450
Plumbum highland’s death squad…

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.530
…crossed the border and
took up position in our village.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:49.460
Their goal was of course to steal
the Simouns from the great temple.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.100
There was no time to lose.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.960
We had to launch the Simouns
and repulse them from the skies.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:01.470
The sibyllae said, “We are
priestesses. We can’t go into battle.”

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.470
The dux turned to
the trainees for volunteers.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.980
Such a thing…

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.150
Tempus Spatium will never allow it.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.490
One such as you
could never fly a Simoun…

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.720
And so I became a sibylla.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:00.280
But only because I was
accomplished in battle.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.300
Otherwise, being of low birth
and having no connections…

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.780
…I would’ve been stripped
of my post right away.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:12.000
If only I could pair up
with Neviril… With Sibylla Aurea…

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.880
Then no one could ever
treat me like an upstart again.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.880
And I could prove there’s
no better sibylla in the world.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.880
But now…

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.120
It’s over.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.640
That’s enough.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.930
That’s not something one
should tell another land’s priestess.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.400
I don’t mind.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:36.130
But anyway, I’m sure keeping
me company is very dull.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.150
Please go about your day freely.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:43.400
Oh? You can take a tour of the ship
as long as it’s not a restricted area.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.280
I’d like that!

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.910
Then as my guide… Do you mind?

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:53.660
It’s Aer, all right? Call me by name.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:43.200
Is it all right to go into
another god’s chapel?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.140
As I mentioned earlier,
the recent theory is that our god…

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:53.470
…was once the same as your
own deity, Tempus Spatium.

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:58.440
Then does that mean your country
used to be a colony of ours?

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.480
Oh, no.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.850
Before Tempus Spatium…

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:06.990
…there may have been
an even more ancient religion.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.330
Aren’t you going to…

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.500
I’m not a priestess.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.240
How could that be?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:24.070
Oh, forget her. She’s just here since
she doesn’t want to go to the Spring.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.760
Praying to gods is trivial.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:30.760
What do you mean? You haven’t
picked a gender yet either, right?

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.350
Well, no, but…

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:41.400
If you’re not sure, forcing an answer
would be even more ridiculous.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.290
A Plumbum dictionary?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.540
Go away.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.170
What’s the problem?
You and I are a pair.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.000
No.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.350
What’s that?

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.260
I’ll check on the conference.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.490
Me too.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.570
Hey, what do you think…

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.980
Those fireworks were a signal.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.920
First, where’s the priestess?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.920
Aer-sama, Sibylla Aurea is…

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.840
She’s got my sister!

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:08.900
Why would she…

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.190
Neviril, what’s this?

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:18.320
It’s as it seems.
This is how they do things.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:21.120
The conference was
a diversion for their infiltration.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.500
To take a Simoun?

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.630
You can’t fly that Simoun, you know!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:30.460
She’s a priestess, right? If there
were two, it might be possible to fly it.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:35.170
If she does, what are those people
in the conference planning to do?

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:39.040
Waporif, block the maintenance
hangar off from the conference room.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.140
Don’t let two highland
priestesses rendezvous!

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.140
Didn’t you hear her? Move it!
We’re blocking all access!

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:50.230
Do you really think
you’re going to pull this off?

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.650
Give it up.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:16:59.830
Big Sister!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:01.910
Alty! Watch out!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.910
Grab her!
Don’t let her touch that Simoun!

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:19.970
Don’t tell me she’s…

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.010
What?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:34.530
If you’re unsure of yourself,
you’ll never find an answer.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.180
Run, Floe.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:37.830
Neviril!

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.120
Right. Bombs!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:39.990
Run, everybody!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.790
She’s got bombs!

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:48.000
Aer!

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.660
What are you…

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.000
But why?

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.260
Nearly all the Simouns
here were destroyed.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.670
We have to see
if the ones spared work…

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.030
Which can fly?

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:47.850
Only the Simouns on the left side.

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:52.810
Only Chor Tempest’s
Simouns, you mean.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.250
Are you all right, Aer?

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:02.080
That girl called out “Aer”…
At the very end…

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.490
What?

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.890
But why? Why my name…

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:09.900
Because it’s not
a person’s name to her.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:13.330
The word “aer” in her own language…

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.840
…means “the highest love of all.”

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:22.830
“Aer” means “the love of god”
in the Plumbum language.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.630
Why?

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.400
Just what is it about this “love of god”?

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.310
How can it make
someone do a thing like that?

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:24.660
Sibylla Aurea,
please fly with me as your pair.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.280
I just heard that Chor Tempest’s
Simouns are the only ones intact.

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:31.290
You’re completely sure
about this, aren’t you?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.790
We don’t have time not to be.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.580
Aer, what will you do?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.770
I don’t know. I just don’t know.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.050
I’m not sure anymore…

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:55.690
Aer, you came here
to fly a Simoun, didn’t you?

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.920
I just don’t want to go to the Spring.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.070
But is that a good thing?

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:09.190
I don’t even have
love of god or anything…

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.010
You needn’t come up with an answer.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.350
I’m unsure too.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.140
About being a priestess.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.850
About going into battle.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:38.860
Whether those are
the right things to do.

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:43.800
You and I are completely
different in every respect.

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:47.360
But we’re alike in just one way.

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:50.240
Stand up, Aer.

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:52.870
I am your pair.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:10.390
One second is enough. Right the ship.
We’re launching the Simouns.

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:12.930
Rubor and Caput were destroyed?

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:15.390
Chor Tempest will be going out.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:47.870
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:52.110
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:59.150
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:06.920
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:19.670
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:24.840
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:28.850
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:32.860
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:38.730
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:44.270
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.700
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:53.370
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:59.770
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:08.460
We will soon be performing…

00:24:08.460 --> 00:24:13.110
…our last Ri Majon as members of
Chor Tempest at the great temple.

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:16.850
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>The Hearing</b>

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.100
The Hearing.
